{{also|от|-от|Appendix:Variations of "ot"}}
==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ru|ото-}} {{i|before certain consonant clusters}}

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*otъ-}}; see {{m|sla-pro|*otъ}} for further information.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|от-|ann=y}} {{i|before vowels, voiceless consonants, voiced resonants and {{lang|ru|в}}}}
* {{ru-IPA|од-|ann=от-}} {{i|before voiced obstruents other than {{lang|ru|в}}}}
* {{ru-IPA|о́т-|ann=y}} {{i|when stressed, before vowels, voiceless consonants, voiced resonants and {{lang|ru|в}}}}
* {{ru-IPA|о́д-|ann=о́т-}} {{i|when stressed, before voiced obstruents other than {{lang|ru|в}}}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|cat2=verbal prefixes}}

# {{lb|ru|used with verbs}} [[away]] [[from]]
#:* {{prefixusex|ru|ходи́ть|pos1=imperfective|t1=to go|отходи́ть|pos2=perfective|t2=to go away}}

====Usage notes====
* Only use от- when the subject moves away from the object of interest, still remaining within a sight range.
:* {{ux|ru|[[я|Я]] [[отойти|отошла́]] [[от]] [[она|неё]].|I walked away from her. (I was standing next to her, but then took a few steps away from her, still being able to see her in the same room or space.)}}
:* {{ux|ru|[[я|Я]] [[уйти|ушла́]] [[от]] [[она|неё]].|I walked away from her. (I was in the same room or space with her, but then left her where she was and went to a different place.)}}

